  "header": "Open weights, private chats, and closer checks on the labs",
  "friendlyHeader": "New AI tools, and a closer look at the companies",
  "summary": "Today's issue is about tools you can use, and about checking the stories around them. Meta has published a very large open-weight model for coding agents. Amazon, Google, Bluesky and Brave are shipping products for notes, shopping, small social projects and encrypted browser chats. Anthropic is embedding outside evaluators, a US regulator has asked two labs for incident files, and a former Meta engineer says one of Anthropic's new systems should have credited an older design.",
  "friendlySummary": "Today we look at tools you can try, and at checks on the companies behind them. Meta released a very large open model for coding. Amazon, Google, Bluesky and Brave added tools for notes, shopping, small projects and private chats. Outside testers are going inside Anthropic. A US regulator has asked two labs for safety files. A former engineer also says one new system should have named the older design it resembles.",
